# madcide layout data (client-server arc V2, 2026-09-09): the shipped
# workbench — WHERE Views live, as data the client owns. The baked default
# (default_layout_text, madcide_core.inc) is this same text as an inline
# profile through the same parser, so a missing or broken file falls back to
# exactly this. Every word converts ONCE at load; a misspelling refuses the
# file with its line.
#
#   @window <name>
#   pane <slot> [<side> <size>%] <mode> views <kind>... [focus] [hidden] [gutter]
#   split <vertical|horizontal> [<size>%]      (children indented beneath)
#   status <top|bottom>                         (the status bar's edge; top)
#   menubar                                     (the menu bar held on top)
#
# slot: editor | sidebar | panel — the editor region is the window's ONE
# slotless child (a pane, or a split of panes: `split vertical` = side by
# side, `split horizontal` = one above the other, any depth); a sidebar docks
# left|right, a panel bottom|top, and neither ever splits. mode: tabs (one
# View behind a strip) | stack (all Views, headers between). kind: source
# code problems output terminal project outline help mdpreview repl. `focus`
# names the pane the keyboard starts in; `hidden` keeps a pane off the screen
# until a command shows it (check surfaces the panel, outline the sidebar) —
# the terminal shows nothing the user did not open. `gutter` gives an editor
# pane line numbers and marks the caret line (a terminal paints them; the
# scheme's gutter / gutter_current / current_line colour them).
@window main
menubar
status bottom
pane editor tabs views source focus gutter
pane sidebar left 20% tabs views outline help mdpreview hidden
pane panel bottom 25% tabs views problems output terminal repl hidden
